From: astrangedaytoday15-dev <342675337+astrangedaytoday15-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:44:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] World 3D S5: window size from the web service, tile export
 into its cache, docs

- The window's size comes from WOWMIN_WORLD3D_TILES on the web service
  (odd 1-7, default 3) through /api/bootstrap instead of a constant in the
  renderer; shown read-only in the panel's toolbar. An open window is
  rebuilt at the new size.
- extract:world now writes into the web service's tile cache
  (<WOWMIN_WORLD_TILE_DIR or assets/world>/v2) by default; before, its
  default folder was one the service never read, so pre-built tiles were
  built again on first visit. --output still writes elsewhere.
- README: World 3D feature, settings, Generating World 3D tiles, Live Map
  usage step.
- Tests: window size edges, CLI output = service cache folder and the two
  cache versions agree.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
