+### Generating World 3D tiles
+
+World 3D builds each open-world tile on first use (needs `WOWMIN_CLIENT_DATA`),
+so this step is optional: it pre-builds the area round a tile, for example
+where your bots level, so a first visit does not wait for it. Tiles go into
+the web service's tile cache (`WOWMIN_WORLD_TILE_DIR`, default
+`assets/world`, in a folder per cache version); `--output` writes elsewhere.
+
+```bash
+# One tile (map 0 = Eastern Kingdoms; X Y are the client's ADT tile numbers)
+npm run extract:world -- --source "/path/to/WoW" --map 0 --tile 32 32
+
+# The 5 x 5 tiles round one tile
+npm run extract:world -- --source "/path/to/WoW" --map 0 --around 32 32 --size 5
+```
+
+A tile with no terrain (open sea) is recorded as empty and drawn as nothing.
+
 #### Classic/TBC dungeon artwork with WDM patches
 
 For proper classic/TBC dungeon floor plans rather than stitched exterior
